---
import './design-aids.css';
import NormalisationTable from './NormalisationTable.astro';
import SketchSheet from './SketchSheet.astro';
import SketchArrow from './SketchArrow.astro';
interface Props { stage: 'rows' | 'partial' | 'transitive'; }
const { stage } = Astro.props;
const titles = {rows:'Give each order line a row',partial:'Move order facts onto the order',transitive:'Give product facts their own table'};
---
<figure id={`normalisation-${stage}`} class="design-aid design-figure paper-surface normal-step wide" aria-labelledby={`normal-${stage}-title`}>
  <span class="plate-number">Illustration · {stage === 'rows' ? 'First normal form' : stage === 'partial' ? 'Second normal form' : 'Third normal form'}</span>
  <h3 id={`normal-${stage}-title`}>{titles[stage]}</h3>
  <p class="key-guide">Underlined columns together form each table’s key. Only the fields needed for this step are shown.</p>
  {stage === 'transitive' && <p class="key-guide">Current catalogue details move to products. Agreed purchase prices stay on the lines.</p>}
  {stage === 'rows' ? <>
    <SketchSheet class="nested-record" tone="blue">
      <p class="stage-label">Starting arrangement · one row per order</p>
      <div class="nested-fields"><div><span>order_id</span><strong>O13</strong></div><div><span>items · a group inside the row</span><div class="nested-items"><div><strong>P7</strong><span>1 mug</span><span>€20 each</span></div><div><strong>P8</strong><span>1 bowl</span><span>€24 each</span></div></div></div></div>
    </SketchSheet>
    <div class="step-arrow"><SketchArrow direction="down" /><p>One row for each item entry.<br />Keep the order ID; give each line a number within that order.</p></div>
    <NormalisationTable label="Purchase lines · one row per entry" columns={['order_id','line_no','product_id','quantity','unit_price']} rows={[[ 'O13','1','P7','1','€20'],['O13','2','P8','1','€24']]} keys={[0,1]} moved={[1]} />
    <figcaption>Both items still belong to O13. The underlined columns form the key: neither order ID nor line number identifies a line alone. A third item adds a row, without changing the columns. Other order details are omitted.</figcaption>
  </> : stage === 'partial' ? <>
    <NormalisationTable label="Before · order details repeated on each line" columns={['order_id','line_no','customer_id','placed_at','product_id']} rows={[[ 'O13','1','C4','10:00','P7'],['O13','2','C4','10:00','P8']]} keys={[0,1]} moved={[2,3]} />
    <div class="dependency"><code>order_id</code><span aria-hidden="true"> → </span><span>customer_id, placed_at</span><small>The order ID alone determines these facts. The line number adds nothing.</small></div>
    <div class="step-arrow"><SketchArrow direction="down" /><p>Store the order details once.<br />Keep order_id on each line to identify its order.</p></div>
    <div class="split-tables">
      <NormalisationTable label="orders" columns={['order_id','customer_id','placed_at']} rows={[[ 'O13','C4','10:00']]} keys={[0]} moved={[1,2]} />
      <NormalisationTable label="order_lines" columns={['order_id','line_no','product_id']} rows={[[ 'O13','1','P7'],['O13','2','P8']]} keys={[0,1]} />
    </div>
    <div class="reference-path"><span aria-hidden="true">↑</span><p>Each O13 line refers to the <strong>same O13 order</strong>.</p></div>
    <figcaption>The highlighted facts depend on part of the original composite key, so they move to a table keyed by that part. Quantities and agreed prices stay on the lines; they are omitted here. “10:00” abbreviates 4 October 2026 at 10:00 UTC.</figcaption>
  </> : <>
    <NormalisationTable label="Before · current product details repeated on lines" columns={['order_id','line_no','product_id','product_name','current_price']} rows={[[ 'O12','1','P7','Blue mug','€20'],['O13','1','P7','Blue mug','€20'],['O13','2','P8','Bowl','€24']]} keys={[0,1]} moved={[3,4]} />
    <div class="dependency"><code>(order_id, line_no)</code><span aria-hidden="true"> → </span><code>product_id</code><span aria-hidden="true"> → </span><span>product_name, current_price</span><small>The line identifies a product; that product determines its current catalogue details.</small></div>
    <div class="step-arrow"><SketchArrow direction="down" /><p>Store catalogue details once per product.<br />Keep product_id on the lines.</p></div>
    <div class="split-tables">
      <NormalisationTable label="products" columns={['product_id','name','current_price']} rows={[[ 'P7','Blue mug','€20'],['P8','Bowl','€24']]} keys={[0]} moved={[1,2]} />
      <NormalisationTable label="order_lines" columns={['order_id','line_no','product_id']} rows={[[ 'O12','1','P7'],['O13','1','P7'],['O13','2','P8']]} keys={[0,1]} />
    </div>
    <div class="reference-path"><span aria-hidden="true">↑</span><p>Both P7 references find <strong>one Blue mug record</strong>.</p></div>
    <figcaption>Product ID is a key in products, but not in order_lines: a product can appear on many lines. Its current details now have one place to change. Quantities and agreed purchase prices remain on the lines, although they are not drawn here.</figcaption>
  </>}
</figure>
<style>
  .normal-step.wide { margin-left:50%; }
  .key-guide { font-size:.78rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .stage-label { font-size:.8rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .normal-step :global(.nested-record) { margin-top:1.5rem; }
  .nested-fields { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 3fr; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); gap:1rem; padding:.8rem 0; }
  .nested-fields > div > span { display:block; font:.75rem var(--font-mono); color:var(--color-text-secondary); margin-bottom:.75rem; }
  .nested-fields strong { font-weight:500; }
  .nested-items { border-left:2px solid var(--teal); padding-left:.8rem; background:var(--paper-match); }
  .nested-items > div { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:.7rem; padding:.6rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule); }
  .step-arrow { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:1rem; margin:1rem 0; }
  .step-arrow > span { color:var(--teal); font:2.8rem var(--font-serif); padding:0 .6rem; }
  .step-arrow p { font-size:.82rem; }
  .split-tables { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr); gap:2rem; align-items:start; }
  .dependency { margin-top:.9rem; border-left:2px solid var(--teal); padding:.2rem .8rem; font-size:.84rem; }
  .dependency > span[aria-hidden] { color:var(--teal); padding:0 .4rem; }
  .dependency small { display:block; color:var(--color-text-secondary); font-size:.75rem; margin-top:.3rem; }
  .reference-path { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:.6rem; font-size:.8rem; margin-top:.4rem; }
  .reference-path > span { color:var(--teal); font-size:1.6rem; }
  @media(max-width:720px) { .split-tables { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:1.2rem; } .nested-fields { grid-template-columns:1fr; } .nested-items > div { flex-wrap:wrap; } }
</style>
